  "label": "Developmental Disability Infantilization",
  "description": "The meme implicitly reinforces the stereotype that individuals with Down syndrome are childlike or incapable of independent decision-making, thereby reducing their personal agency. The framing of the image as 'amusing' or 'pity-inducing' suggests that their actions are not to be taken seriously, which infantilizes them and denies their autonomy.",
